Then we're bound to be inconsistent on many occasions.  Nick still
hasn't answered my question why he mapped _Oesterreich_ to {.e-} but
_Tu"rkiye_ to {-u-}, given that the two vowels differ only in height.

>  Preservation of the written form is desirable, and can resolve such
>  problems.

Yes.  That's what {la'o} is for.

>  For country and city names, this
